{"id":"kenaz","name":"Kenaz","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:kenaz"],"types":[{"type":"person","from":"UBS: Names of People"}],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Kenaz","text":"Hunter. (1.) One of the sons of Eliphaz, the son of Esau. He became the chief of an Edomitish tribe (Gen. 36:11, 15, 42). (2.) Caleb’s younger brother, and father of Othniel (Josh. 15:17), whose family was of importance in Israel down to the time of David (1 Chr. 27:15). Some think that Othniel (Judg. 1:13), and not Kenaz, was Caleb’s brother. (3.) Caleb’s grandson (1 Chr. 4:15)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7073","lemma":"קְנַז","xlit":"Qᵉnaz","gloss":"Kenaz, the name of an Edomite and of two Israelites","kjv":"Kenaz","count":10,"share":0.83},{"strong":"H441","lemma":"אַלּוּף","xlit":"ʼallûwph","gloss":"familiar","kjv":"captain, duke, friend, governor","count":3,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":8,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H251","lemma":"אָח","xlit":"ʼâch","gloss":"a brother )","kjv":"another, brother; kindred, like, other","count":3,"share":0.25}],"verses":["Gen.36.11","Gen.36.15","Gen.36.42","Josh.15.17","Judg.1.13","Judg.3.9","Judg.3.11","1Chr.1.36","1Chr.1.53","1Chr.4.13","1Chr.4.0","1Chr.15.0"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"othniel","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.25,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"omar","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.25,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"zepho","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.25,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"duke","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.068,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"duke","type":"lexical","strong":"H441","why":"both lead with אַלּוּף (H441)"},{"id":"e